# How credit is recorded: governance/credit-and-authorship.md. Release manifests (releases/vX.Y.Z/RELEASE.yaml, `contributors`) list maintainers and contributors with
# their roles.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SCALE, please cite the software release and the accompanying article."
title: "SCALE — Shared Concepts, Attributes, and Links with Evidence (scale-schema reference implementation)"
version: 0.1.0
# date-released is set when a release is built (governance/release-process.md, step 3); none has been built yet, so
# this describes the development version 0.1.0.
# license: the software's licence (the code). The vocabulary, curated records and documentation are CC-BY-4.0
# (REUSE.toml, NOTICE, governance/licensing.md). CFF 1.2.0 states no way to say that two licences apply
# together (it does not define a list of licences as "all of"), so only the software's is given.
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "SCALE contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hlxin/scale"
keywords: [knowledge graph, provenance, evidence, schema evolution, FAIR, agents, catalysis]
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "SCALE: Shared Concepts, Attributes, and Links with Evidence"
  authors:
    - name: "SCALE authors (manuscript in preparation)"
  status: in-preparation
